@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Microsoft YaHei
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title SIM-ddd-sequence — source snapshot (not a runtime trace)
participant "obj: 调用者" as obj
participant "ctl: AuthorizationController" as ctl
participant "rest: RestSupport" as rest
participant "auth: AuthorizationApplicationService" as auth
participant "directory: DirectoryApplicationService" as directory
participant "repo: AuthorizationRepository" as repo
activate obj
obj -> ctl: 1. explain(bearer, input)
activate ctl
ctl -> ctl: 2. check(bearer, input, true)
activate ctl
ctl -> rest: 3. principal(bearer)
activate rest
deactivate rest
ctl -> auth: 4. require(principal, rbac:authz:invoke, false)
activate auth
deactivate auth
note over ctl
Validate UI permission vs API operationId input contract;
choose explicit target userId or actor.id().
end note
opt target differs from actor
ctl -> directory: 5. user(principal, targetUserId)
activate directory
deactivate directory
end
ctl -> auth: 6. unavailableReason(targetUserId, system)
activate auth
auth -> repo: 7. systemEnabled(system)
activate repo
deactivate repo
auth -> repo: 8. identity(targetUserId)
activate repo
deactivate repo
alt missing target
auth --> obj: 404 USER_NOT_FOUND; abort
else existing target
note over auth
non-ACTIVE → USER_DISABLED; otherwise disabled system → SYSTEM_DISABLED;
active user + enabled system → null
end note
end
auth --> ctl: unavailable
deactivate auth
alt unavailable != null
note over ctl
empty effective; allowed=false; reason=unavailable;
explain trace=[ACTOR_AUTHENTICATED, unavailable]; fresh traceId.
No effective()/api() call for unavailable target.
end note
else available target
ctl -> auth: 9. effective(targetUserId, system)
activate auth
deactivate auth
opt API decision
ctl -> auth: 10. api(targetUserId, system, operationId)
activate auth
deactivate auth
end
note over ctl
UI uses Effective.has; reason ALLOW or DENY;
explain trace records TOKEN_VALID, USER_SYSTEM_ACTIVE and requirement result
end note
end
note over ctl
RestSupport.ok supplies HTTP envelope; target disabled is a DENY result,
not authentication failure of the requesting administrator.
No business mutation or SUCCESS audit occurs in this simulation.
end note
deactivate ctl
deactivate ctl
deactivate obj
@enduml